<!--
  Alternate-language annotations, the fourth of the Google sitemap extensions.

  Unlike news, image and video, hreflang has no namespace of its own: the links are xhtml:link
  elements in the XHTML namespace, which is why the extension's prefix is xhtml rather than something
  sitemap-shaped.

  Two things a reader has to get right and a single-link document never tests. First, the annotation
  is reciprocal — every url in a set lists every alternate including itself, so the three entries here
  each carry three links, not two. Second, x-default is a valid hreflang value and is not a language
  code; treating it as one produces a culture parse failure on a document Google considers correct.

  endjin publishes in English. The locale paths exist to exercise the extension, and are not a claim
  that endjin serves translated pages.
-->
